<p>San Antonio homes are built for heat, not hard freezes. Water lines often run through attics, exterior walls, and slab penetrations with limited insulation, and many homes have hose bibs and plumbing on north-facing walls. When temperatures stay below freezing for days, pipes split. Then the thaw comes, and the water pours out.</p>

